Article 2 (Institutions Eligible to Borrow Artifacts) The Director of the National Museum of Korea, directors of its affiliated regional museums, the Director of the National Folk Museum of Korea, and the Director of the National Museum of Korean Contemporary History (hereinafter referred to as "museum directors") may lend artifacts held by their respective museums (hereinafter referred to as "museum-held artifacts") to any of the following institutions to the extent that such lending does not interfere with the performance of their duties: <Amended on May 10, 2013>
1. National museums and national art museums under the Museum and Art Museum Support Act, and museums or art museums registered under Article 16 (1) of that Act;
2. National science museums, public science museums, and registered science museums under the Science Museums Promotion Act;
3. Museums, art museums, and science museums attached to schools of various levels under the Lifelong Education Act;
4. Other museums, art museums, and science museums deemed appropriate by a museum director.
